  "content_blocks": [
    {
      "block_id": "b00000",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Navigating the Procurement Act 2023",
      "ordinal": 0,
      "heading_path": [
        "Navigating the Procurement Act 2023"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00001",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Legislative Structure",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "heading_path": [
        "Navigating the Procurement Act 2023",
        "Legislative Structure"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00002",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The new procurement regime is made up of primary legislation (the Procurement Act 2023 ) and of secondary legislation that sits under it, in particular, the Procurement Regulations 2024 (although further secondary legislation is likely to be made in due course).",
      "ordinal": 2,
      "heading_path": [
        "Navigating the Procurement Act 2023",
        "Legislative Structure"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00003",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Transitional Provisions",
      "ordinal": 3,
      "heading_path": [
        "Navigating the Procurement Act 2023",
        "Legislative Structure",
        "Transitional Provisions"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00004",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The new regime applies to all regulated contracts whose procurement was commenced on or after 24 February 2025 . Generally, a procurement will be commenced on the date that the contract notice/advertisement is published.",
      "ordinal": 4,
      "heading_path": [
        "Navigating the Procurement Act 2023",
        "Legislative Structure",
        "Transitional Provisions"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00005",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "More detailed government guidance on transition is available here .",
      "ordinal": 5,
      "heading_path": [
        "Navigating the Procurement Act 2023",
        "Legislative Structure",
        "Transitional Provisions"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00006",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Contracts whose procurement was commenced before 24 February 2025 will continue to be regulated by the Public Contracts Regulations 2015 (or where relevant by the equivalent Utilities/Defence/Concessions regulations). This includes where modifications are made to the contract after 24 February 2025.",
      "ordinal": 6,
      "heading_path": [
        "Navigating the Procurement Act 2023",
        "Legislative Structure",
        "Transitional Provisions"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00007",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Where the procurement of a framework agreement or dynamic purchasing system was commenced before 24 February 2025, then that agreement and all contracts called off under it, will remained regulated by the \"old\" regime - even after 24 February 2025.",
      "ordinal": 7,
      "heading_path": [
        "Navigating the Procurement Act 2023",
        "Legislative Structure",
        "Transitional Provisions"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00008",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Anatomy of the Act",
      "ordinal": 8,
      "heading_path": [
        "Navigating the Procurement Act 2023",
        "Legislative Structure",
        "Anatomy of the Act"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00009",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The Act is intended to make sense in terms of its structure; beginning with core principles and pre-procurement, through to procurement, award, contract management, and remedies and oversight.",
      "ordinal": 9,
      "heading_path": [
        "Navigating the Procurement Act 2023",
        "Legislative Structure",
        "Anatomy of the Act"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00010",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Below you can find our commentary on each \"part\" of the Act, following the narrative arc of a procurement process.",
      "ordinal": 10,
      "heading_path": [
        "Navigating the Procurement Act 2023",
        "Legislative Structure",
        "Anatomy of the Act"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00011",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Part 1: Key definitions Part 1 of the Procurement Act covers key definitions and outlines the regime's scope. View part one",
      "ordinal": 11,
      "heading_path": [
        "Navigating the Procurement Act 2023",
        "Legislative Structure",
        "Anatomy of the Act"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00012",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Part 2: Principles and objectives Part 2 of the Act details the core principles and objectives that are to shape contracting authority approaches to procurement practice. View part two",
      "ordinal": 12,
      "heading_path": [
        "Navigating the Procurement Act 2023",
        "Legislative Structure",
        "Anatomy of the Act"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00013",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Part 3: Award of public contracts and procedures Part 3 forms the main body of the Act, focussing on the award of public contracts and the procedures involved, ensuring that the process is fair, transparent, and efficient. View part three",
      "ordinal": 13,
      "heading_path": [
        "Navigating the Procurement Act 2023",
        "Legislative Structure",
        "Anatomy of the Act"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00014",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Part 4: Management of public contracts Part 4 of the Procurement Act deals with the management of public contracts. View part four",
      "ordinal": 14,
      "heading_path": [
        "Navigating the Procurement Act 2023",
        "Legislative Structure",
        "Anatomy of the Act"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00015",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Parts 5 - 7: Conflicts of interest, contracts & obligations Parts 5, 6 & 7 covers conflicts of interest, below-threshold contracts, and international obligations, introducing new requirements and concepts to enhance transparency and compliance. View parts five to seven",
      "ordinal": 15,
      "heading_path": [
        "Navigating the Procurement Act 2023",
        "Legislative Structure",
        "Anatomy of the Act"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00016",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Part 8: Information and notices Part 8 of the Procurement Act deals with transparency, notices and record-keeping to ensure accountability. Part 8: Information and notices",
      "ordinal": 16,
      "heading_path": [
        "Navigating the Procurement Act 2023",
        "Legislative Structure",
        "Anatomy of the Act"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00017",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Part 9: Remedies for breach of statutory duty Part 9 outlines remedies for breaches of statutory duty, including formal challenges in the High Court, automatic suspensions during the standstill period, and contract set-aside provisions View part nine",
      "ordinal": 17,
      "heading_path": [
        "Navigating the Procurement Act 2023",
        "Legislative Structure",
        "Anatomy of the Act"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00018",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Part 10: Procurement oversight Part 10 of the Procurement Act introduces the Procurement Review Unit, with focus on debarment, supplier complaint, and systemic and institutional non-compliance. View part ten",
      "ordinal": 18,
      "heading_path": [
        "Navigating the Procurement Act 2023",
        "Legislative Structure",
        "Anatomy of the Act"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
